    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Shipwreck | Subclass: Wooden\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a wood shipwreck. Identified as the Foss Barge 54. Resting in 15 feet of water and measuring roughly 91 feet by 26 feet. Visable large deck beams and structural members still largely intact along with upright structures extending upwards to the surface. There are holes into the interrior of the wreck that were not explored by some viewable debris can be seen such as car tire. The Foss 54 was originally built in 1908 for the U.S. Navy in Bremerton, Washington. Multiple sources indicate the barges use, from coal transport, lumber transport, to other materials from the region the barge Puget Sound served for almost 60 years. In 1969 it was removed from documentaiton and presumably sinks shortly after that time. \nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey classified this target as LU07. Described as a barge and the wreck of a Foss 54 in Lake Union. Previously, DCS Films classified this target as Foss 54. DCS films provides details about the vessel including historic photos. Previously, Lake Union Virtual Museum classified this target as the wreck as the Foss 54.",
