    location: "Lake Union, Seattle",
    status: "recently-explored",
    tagline: "This target has been classified as man made debris.",
    summary: "Type: Debris | Class: Man Made | Subclass: Mixed Materials\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as man made debris. Resting in 40 feet of water. Debris field contains large tire partially embedded in silt near a large squared timber, likely a piling or bollard, with a metal ring or eye fitting set into its top and a length of chain or rope looped through it. Scattered debris, including what appears to be a can and other discarded items, surrounds the site.\nPrior Research and Theories\nThis target has been classified by Coastal Sensing & Survey as LU11, described the same way.",
