    coordinates: [47.6392968, -122.3390021],
    location: "Lake Union, Seattle",
    status: "recently-explored",
    tagline: "This target has been classified as a wooden barge, resting in 40 feet of water.",
    summary: "Shipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a wooden barge, resting in 40 feet of water. Shipwreck City's own measurements put the vessel at roughly 60 feet by 20 feet. The hull structure remains largely intact, with visible deck beams, joints, and at least one upright post or piling rising from the frame, possibly a bit or mooring point. Sponge-like yellow biofouling colonizes much of the exposed wood, and patches of aquatic weeds have taken hold across sections of the deck and beams. A length of rope or cable is visible coiled and wrapped around parts of the structure. \nPrior Research and Theories\nThis target has been logged twice by Coastal Sensing & Survey under LU32: an initial entry from January 28, 2020 recorded as an unknown barge, and a follow up from August 22, 2021 noting the barge's well preserved structure in more recent imagery, with a recorded dimension of 45 feet by 16 feet, smaller than the figure from Shipwreck City's own survey. It has also been referenced as \"Barge #3\" in DCS Films' Lake Union wreck survey, though without additional written detail.",
    summarySections: [{heading: "Shipwreck City Data", body: "This target has been classified as a wooden barge, resting in 40 feet of water. Shipwreck City's own measurements put the vessel at roughly 60 feet by 20 feet. The hull structure remains largely intact, with visible deck beams, joints, and at least one upright post or piling rising from the frame, possibly a bit or mooring point. Sponge-like yellow biofouling colonizes much of the exposed wood, and patches of aquatic weeds have taken hold across sections of the deck and beams. A length of rope or cable is visible coiled and wrapped around parts of the structure."}, {heading: "Prior Research and Theories", body: "This target has been logged twice by Coastal Sensing & Survey under LU32: an initial entry from January 28, 2020 recorded as an unknown barge, and a follow up from August 22, 2021 noting the barge's well preserved structure in more recent imagery, with a recorded dimension of 45 feet by 16 feet, smaller than the figure from Shipwreck City's own survey. It has also been referenced as \"Barge #3\" in DCS Films' Lake Union wreck survey, though without additional written detail."}],
