    tagline: "This target has been classified as a 45 foot wooden boat, resting in 40 feet of water, with a dimension of 45 feet by 16 feet.",
    summary: "Shipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a 45 foot wooden boat, resting in 40 feet of water, with a dimension of 45 feet by 16 feet. Possible name lettering reading \"Crooery Ark\" is visible on the hull, though the wording is not fully legible. The wreckage is broken apart, with sonar imagery showing a scattered debris field alongside the more intact sections of hull. ROV footage shows structural timbers crossing over one another at the site, along with what appears to be a mast step or deck fitting encrusted with growth, sitting between crossed planks. Additional metal hardware, including a small cylindrical fitting with visible threading, was also observed among the wreckage.\nPrior Research and Theories\nThis target has been logged twice by Coastal Sensing & Survey under LU33: an initial entry from January 28, 2020 describing it as an unknown boat, mostly reduced to debris, with possible name lettering reading \"Crooery Ark,\" and a follow up entry from August 22, 2021 describing it simply as an old wreck with an interesting sonar return.\nAdditional Context\nThis target has not been historically identified. The partial name lettering, if confirmed, could offer a path to identifying the vessel through historical vessel registries or newspaper archives, though \"Crooery Ark\" does not correspond to any known wreck or vessel name found so far.",
