    tagline: "This target has been classified as a wooden shipwreck, recently explored by the Shipwreck City team in May 2026.",
    summary: "Shipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a wooden shipwreck, recently explored by the Shipwreck City team in May 2026. The hull is broken apart, with exact dimensions still to be determined given the collapsed state of the structure. ROV footage shows scattered structural timbers, including planking crossed in an X-pattern near the wreck site, and a length of corroded metal rod or hardware — possibly a stanchion or deck fitting — still upright among the wood. A separate section of curved hull or framing sits partially buried in silt, with a small metal or ceramic fitting nearby. Visibility at the site was poor, consistent with typical Lake Union conditions, and no fish or significant marine growth are clearly visible in the frames captured.\nPrior Research and Theories\nThis target has been linked to a prior Coastal Sensing & Survey record logged as an \"Unknown Sailboat,\" surveyed by diver Ben Griner on January 28, 2020.\nAdditional Context\nThis target has not been historically identified. Its broken-apart, unidentified state is consistent with many of the smaller work boats and derelict craft that make up much of Lake Union's wreck population.",
